{"chunk_id": "639c650f5f70", "text": "Arjuna resists a proposal he sees as sinful and urges that Draupadi be properly married according to virtue and seniority. Yet after the brothers gaze upon Draupadi, her extraordinary beauty stirs desire in all of them. Yudhishthira perceives the tension and, recalling Vyasa\u2019s words and fearing division among the brothers, declares that Draupadi will be the common wife of all five Pandavas. Soon after, Krishna and Balarama secretly visit the disguised brothers in the potter\u2019s house, recognizing their true identity despite their concealment and offering quiet encouragement. Meanwhile Dhrishtadyumna secretly observes their humble domestic life, where Kunti instructs Draupadi in household duties. His report to King Drupada begins to reveal that the mysterious Brahmins who won Draupadi are in fact the Pandavas, setting the stage for a politically and morally unusual marriage.\nYudhishthira decides Draupadi will be the common wife of the five brothers, while Krishna secretly meets the disguised Pandavas and Dhrishtadyumna spies on them.\nThemes: polyandry decision, brotherly unity, divine recognition, concealed identity, family hierarchy", "vector": [-0.005764653906226158, -0.030102072283625603, -0.008636938408017159, -0.00505495211109519, -9.169423719868064e-05, 0.020393887534737587, -0.02252299152314663, 0.011047246865928173, -0.0067187342792749405, -0.02978069894015789, -0.0026094934437423944, -0.0013934595044702291, 0.004529370926320553, 0.004465765785425901, -0.008978398516774178, 0.019670793786644936, 0.04204649105668068, -0.013303562998771667, 0.029137950390577316, -0.026031330227851868, -0.004308426287025213, -0.01771576702594757, -0.011549393646419048, 0.013089313171803951, -0.030718041583895683, 0.03128044679760933, 0.016952501609921455, -0.026915110647678375, -0.0025944290682673454, 0.005778044927865267, -0.008456164970993996, -0.001749147311784327, 0.007806720677763224, -0.007351440377533436, -0.0380828715860843